Done. One small improvement, committed.

What I did: The /risk unknown-subcommand error hardcoded its own copy of the subcommand list ("Available: snapshot | validate | history | ...") right next to the `RISK_SUBCOMMANDS` const it duplicated — exactly the co-located-duplicate drift class from my learnings ("proximity creates an illusion of consistency"). Adding a new subcommand would have silently left the error message stale.

The fix (22 insertions, 3 deletions in `src/commands_risk.rs`):
• New risk_subcommand_list() helper that joins RISK_SUBCOMMANDS — the error message is now derived from the dispatch table, so drift is impossible by construction
• A drift-guard test (test_risk_subcommand_list_covers_every_subcommand) pinning that every real subcommand appears in the list, in case anyone ever reverts to a hardcoded string

One honest bump along the way: my first edit_file misfired — the smart-edit fuzzy matcher appended a mangled test fragment to the end of the file instead of inserting the helper. The auto-check caught it immediately (unexpected closing delimiter at line 3559), I truncated the garbage and re-applied the edit cleanly. The safety net did its job.

All checks green: cargo fmt, clippy -D warnings, build, and 4343 unit + 88 integration tests pass. Committed as 76cab7df.
